<<~ ahu #/operator-howto>>
!! Do it, inspect it, steer it

From repo root, switch to the PR branch, then enter tools/projection-loom:

```bash
git fetch origin
git switch feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--projection-loom
git pull --ff-only
cd tools/projection-loom
python -m pip install -r requirements-ci.txt
python -m pip install --no-deps -e .
python -m pytest -q tests
python -m projection_loom ooda-run --project examples/necrospire/project.json --capability-recipe examples/necrospire/hybrid/recipe.json --out out/necrospire-compound --control full-speed --passes 3 --candidates 4 --exact-budget 3 --detail-budget 3 --score-size 128 192 --finalists 3
python scripts/check_compound_epoch.py --out out/necrospire-compound
python -m projection_loom ooda-status --session out/necrospire-compound/session.json
```

Read out/necrospire-compound/previews/epoch_NNN/review.json and
out/necrospire-compound/finalists/gallery.json and contact_sheet.png.
Review exact CAD, polygons, source provenance and socket receipts separately.

For an operator-guided voyage, use --control manual and a NEW out directory.
At a checkpoint issue `ooda-steer --session OUT/session.json --action approve-plan`,
then rerun the SAME initial `ooda-run` command; repeat for review gates.
Use `--action review`, `--action pause`, `--action set-autonomy --autonomy 0.4`,
or `--action open-inquiry --loop epoch-0001 --question "What connects?"`.
An inquiry advances through `--action advance-inquiry --loop ID --phase PHASE
--note TEXT`. To pet-name a reviewed entity, provide the actual proposal and
@entity/Crystal witness handle using `--action pet-name --proposal ID --target
@entity/Crystal --name "Crystal with Opinions"`. Use `--action choose --proposal
ID` to steer a validated lineage; use `--action o-takiage --name "Crystal with
Opinions"` to release the hold without erasing its history. Operator controls
apply at safe phase boundaries, not inside uninterruptible CAD kernel calls.

For a locally installed LLM, add `--llm-provider ollama --llm-model MODEL`;
for a trusted OpenAI-compatible service use `--llm-provider openai-compatible
--llm-model MODEL` with the documented endpoint and OPENAI_API_KEY environment
variable. No provider may choose outside verified previews or waive gates.

For the CC0 hard reference, run `python scripts/fetch_references.py --source
brutalism2 --cache .ref-cache --lockfile references.lock.local.json
--bootstrap-lock`; review digest/license/contents before promoting the lock.
For Ur, honor official downloaded-archive/OAuth flows and attribution.

<<~/ahu>>

